&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A program already running a window&amp;rsquo;s loop cannot give &lt;code&gt;Run&lt;/code&gt; its main thread:
&lt;code&gt;Attach&lt;/code&gt; puts the same icon up and returns, and &lt;code&gt;Quit&lt;/code&gt; takes it down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The native back-ends are on by default; there is no build tag to remember.
On a platform with none, &lt;code&gt;Run&lt;/code&gt; returns &lt;code&gt;ErrNoBackend&lt;/code&gt; — the difference
between &amp;ldquo;there is no tray here&amp;rdquo; and a tray that silently does nothing. A test
or a headless service passes &lt;code&gt;WithBackend(tray.NewHeadless())&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>